      "writtenOn": "2026-06-11T10:02:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So if we have a `MTLPixelFormatR16Unorm` texture that\u0027s backed by an `x420` IOSurface, it will be sampled differently than a `MTLPixelFormatR16Unorm` that isn\u0027t?\n\nThat\u0027s fairly shocking... it would have been better to have had a dedicated pixel format for this sort of thing (like `VK_FORMAT_R10X6_UNORM_PACK16`). That also really complicates the implementation. If we could infer behavior from the pixel format then the fix would be simpler.",
      "revId": "465305d6059e39b59a15dd87796fbd6dce2149ff",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18e44135_dd8be4d7",
